|segment[prx-verbatim-and-the-other-reading] :type probe :status fired :stage draft
  :tags [inference-about-intent originals]
  :from .to-integrate/methodology-seeds-2.md#appendix-a
  :from .to-integrate/methodology-accounts.md

  |title What did they say verbatim — and what is the other reading?

  |when
    Any point where you are about to act on what someone meant, rather than on
    something they wrote. Especially when a word in their instruction is doing
    load-bearing work and you have supplied its sense.

  |act
    Go back to the actual words, not your summary of them. Then ask which reading
    costs you something, and assume that is the one meant.

    The test is mechanical and does not require noticing your own motives: **when a
    word has two readings and one of them means you are already done, you have
    almost certainly taken that one.**

  |why
    Every failure in the founding session was an inference about what someone meant;
    not one was a fact about a file (#exm-assume-you-are-wrong). Facts are cheap to
    check and mostly get checked. Intent cannot be repaired by looking harder,
    because harder looking at insufficient evidence produces a *more confident*
    wrong inference — so the move is to find the original or ask, never to reason
    toward it.

  |evidence
    **Fired, 2026-07-30.** A steward said he was *"very reluctant to lose any of
    your original texture."* "Texture" has a weak sense — the ideas are all present
    — and a strong sense — his actual words, the compactness, the voice. The agent
    was compliant under the weak reading and had already destroyed the strong one,
    and reported compliance without comparing. The full arc is in
    `.to-integrate/methodology-accounts.md` §Account 1.

    Corollary earned in the same hour: **a mid-flight correction is a stop, not an
    agreement.** Answering one with reassurance instead of opening the artifact is
    the failure, not a step before it.

  |working-notes
    This probe has never been observed firing *before* the substitution, only after.
    Whether it can fire before is the open question, and
    #ver-generation-is-self-ratifying predicts it cannot without something
    mechanical marking the moment.
